WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
Captain Video!

00:04.000 --> 00:08.000
Captain Video!

00:08.000 --> 00:12.000
Electronic wizard!

00:12.000 --> 00:16.000
Master of power and space! Guardian of the

00:16.000 --> 00:20.000
safety of the world!

00:20.000 --> 00:24.000
Waiting for law and order, Captain Video operates from a

00:24.000 --> 00:28.000
mountain retreat with secret agents at all points of the

00:28.000 --> 00:32.000
globe. Possessing scientific secrets and scientific weapons,

00:32.000 --> 00:36.000
Captain Video asks no quarter and gives

00:36.000 --> 00:40.000
none to the forces of evil. Stand by for

00:40.000 --> 00:44.000
Captain Video!

00:44.000 --> 00:48.000
And here's Video Rangers!

00:48.000 --> 00:52.000
Music

00:52.000 --> 00:56.000
Last time Video Rangers, you'll remember

00:56.000 --> 01:00.000
that some startling developments took place on two planets many

01:00.000 --> 01:04.000
light years apart. On Metasteros, you saw Captain

01:04.000 --> 01:08.000
Video preside over an interplanetary meeting, and you watched him give

01:08.000 --> 01:12.000
Sita of Mars a few lessons in the art of physical combat.

01:12.000 --> 01:16.000
Meanwhile, back on Earth, you saw Dr.

01:16.000 --> 01:20.000
Pauly in action again, making his sinister plots to rule the

01:20.000 --> 01:24.000
world. Now let's get right into today's story. As we

01:24.000 --> 01:28.000
go to the headquarters of Permes Lycos on Metasteros.

01:28.000 --> 01:32.000
Hi there, Captain. Nice. Yeah,

01:32.000 --> 01:36.000
that's alright, Ranger. I have to get through that with you.

01:36.000 --> 01:40.000
Feel a little something in these knuckles? Boy, you're going to use that hand, boy.

01:40.000 --> 01:44.000
Well, now that we've settled our personal differences, supposedly you get down to business.

01:44.000 --> 01:48.000
That suits me fine. I've had all I want of personal business.

01:48.000 --> 01:52.000
I should think so, speaker.

01:52.000 --> 01:56.000
What do you suggest is the correct treatment for our person? Well, Captain, we

01:56.000 --> 02:00.000
feel that the permanent regulations must be applied. To what

02:00.000 --> 02:04.000
extent? Well, to begin with, occupation of person by the

02:04.000 --> 02:08.000
permanent police. Also, all communication with other planets

02:08.000 --> 02:12.000
to be subjected to strict censorship. And trade with other planets

02:12.000 --> 02:16.000
to be restricted.

02:16.000 --> 02:20.000
What else? Well, a change in the

02:20.000 --> 02:24.000
position of the permanent to an orbit that can be kept under constant watch.

02:24.000 --> 02:28.000
Naturally, all weapons of person to be confiscated

02:28.000 --> 02:32.000
and destroyed. Each personarium

02:32.000 --> 02:36.000
will be required to spend a full-time cycle

02:36.000 --> 02:40.000
and farm labor. The product to be given to a peaceful

02:40.000 --> 02:44.000
planet. Right? Right. As a little

02:44.000 --> 02:48.000
estimate, the regulations are just what we've done for Aeon.

02:48.000 --> 02:52.000
Gentlemen, all I know is that if you want to create everlasting hatred,

02:52.000 --> 02:56.000
to make slaves to be a defeated enemy.

02:56.000 --> 03:00.000
And that's all that these terms would accomplish, the way I see it.

03:00.000 --> 03:04.000
Well then, what you seem to be in favor of is

03:04.000 --> 03:08.000
Earth policy, eh, Captain Video? To a degree, yes, I do.

03:08.000 --> 03:12.000
Well, Captain, what do you

03:12.000 --> 03:16.000
suggest we do? I suggest a much more moderate

03:16.000 --> 03:20.000
policy. Terson is a defeated enemy, yes, but don't forget

03:20.000 --> 03:24.000
she's a member of the same firmament. We all are, for that matter.

03:24.000 --> 03:28.000
I don't like this business about

03:28.000 --> 03:32.000
confiscating the weapons. For years, Mars has had a very

03:32.000 --> 03:36.000
profitable trade agreement with war materials with

03:36.000 --> 03:40.000
Terson. I

03:40.000 --> 03:44.000
withdraw the stake.

03:44.000 --> 03:48.000
As he grows older, Tita grows

03:48.000 --> 03:52.000
wiser. Gentlemen, suppose we all sit down.

03:52.000 --> 03:56.000
Yes. Let us. Now I suggest

03:56.000 --> 04:00.000
a much more moderate policy.

04:00.000 --> 04:04.000
Why wouldn't it be perfectly reasonable?

04:04.000 --> 04:08.000
So give Terson a new place in the orbit. Let her have

04:08.000 --> 04:12.000
room to expand, room to breathe, as Regis put it.

04:12.000 --> 04:16.000
Captain Video, they'll think of it as a sign of weakness.

04:16.000 --> 04:20.000
I don't think they will, Ventura. They will,

04:20.000 --> 04:24.000
they'll misinterpret it if they do. Don't forget that we're still

04:24.000 --> 04:28.000
strong enough to give orders and see who they carry it out.

04:28.000 --> 04:32.000
What do you say, Colonel?

04:32.000 --> 04:36.000
I'm with you, Captain. What say you all?

04:36.000 --> 04:40.000
Agreed. Agreed.

04:40.000 --> 04:44.000
Good. What do you say to this plan, Captain?

04:44.000 --> 04:48.000
You and the Video Ranger go to Terson as our ambassador of good will.

04:48.000 --> 04:52.000
Then you can bring our decision to Regis himself. And then return here with any

04:52.000 --> 04:56.000
further recommendations he might care to make.

04:56.000 --> 05:00.000
That's all right with me. I'd be perfectly happy to do it. All right with you, gentlemen.

05:00.000 --> 05:04.000
Good. Fine. How about you, Ranger?

05:04.000 --> 05:08.000
Okay with me, sir. All right.

05:08.000 --> 05:12.000
Mediceiros,

05:12.000 --> 05:16.000
calling Terson. Firmly Bichos,

05:16.000 --> 05:20.000
calling Regis of Terson. Regis in demand.

05:20.000 --> 05:24.000
This is Regis of Terson. Regis,

05:24.000 --> 05:28.000
Captain Video and the Video Ranger are coming to visit you. Bring our decision.

05:28.000 --> 05:32.000
And the last is our Special Emissary. I shall

05:32.000 --> 05:36.000
welcome your Captain Video. This is

05:36.000 --> 05:40.000
Regis signing off. Firmly Bichos signing off.

05:40.000 --> 05:44.000
Did you hear that

05:44.000 --> 05:48.000
signal? Captain Video is coming here.

05:48.000 --> 05:52.000
Must have a plan. We must set a track for him.

05:52.000 --> 05:56.000
We must never see that beautiful

05:56.000 --> 06:00.000
earth of his again. We'd have had

06:00.000 --> 06:04.000
Mediceiros right now if it hadn't have been for him. And I know what that

06:04.000 --> 06:08.000
terms will be. Yes. Yes, so do I.

06:08.000 --> 06:12.000
An abject surrender.

06:12.000 --> 06:16.000
Slave labor.

06:16.000 --> 06:20.000
For that fat Fermi of Jupiter to make him all the fatter.

06:20.000 --> 06:24.000
And I won't put up with it.

06:24.000 --> 06:28.000
I would rather die first than see Terson destroyed.

06:28.000 --> 06:32.000
Captain Video will undoubtedly arrive in an

06:32.000 --> 06:36.000
out of control run.

06:36.000 --> 06:40.000
He will land at the usual stage.

06:40.000 --> 06:44.000
Perhaps we can arrange a surprise.

06:44.000 --> 06:48.000
Of course.

06:48.000 --> 06:52.000
Captain Video, may I speak with you for a moment?

06:52.000 --> 06:56.000
Certainly. I would like to have

06:56.000 --> 07:00.000
you pay me a visit on Mars. I'd certainly be very happy

07:00.000 --> 07:04.000
to do that. Why in particular would you like me to come?

07:04.000 --> 07:08.000
I'd like you to teach my soldiers how to kill men with their bare

07:08.000 --> 07:12.000
fists.

07:12.000 --> 07:16.000
See that? Never leave with your right. You're a sucker for

07:16.000 --> 07:20.000
a right cross. I see.

07:20.000 --> 07:24.000
You know, Cedar, on earth we consider boxing a sport. It teaches

07:24.000 --> 07:28.000
you how to defend yourself. It teaches you good

07:28.000 --> 07:32.000
sportsmanship. It teaches you skill. It teaches you how to avoid right crosses too.

07:32.000 --> 07:36.000
Oh, one thing more.

07:36.000 --> 07:40.000
No mention must be made of our little

07:40.000 --> 07:44.000
match on Mars. Don't worry. It's strictly between you and me.

07:44.000 --> 07:48.000
An excellent conference, but

07:48.000 --> 07:52.000
one problem with it though, it kept me from these luscious Jupiter grapes.

07:52.000 --> 07:56.000
Well, farewell, Fermi.

07:56.000 --> 08:00.000
Farewell. Farewell, Fermi. Farewell, Benjona.

08:00.000 --> 08:04.000
Farewell, Ranger. Cedar.

08:04.000 --> 08:08.000
And now,

08:08.000 --> 08:12.000
we must make some necessary arrangements for your trip to Tartan.

08:12.000 --> 08:16.000
Well, first I'd like to contact Earth. I'd like to

08:16.000 --> 08:20.000
tell them what's been going on here. Yeah, I'd like to

08:20.000 --> 08:24.000
find out what's been going on down there. So would I, Ranger. Well, tell me, do you wish to use

08:24.000 --> 08:28.000
the rocket technique, Captain, or rely on the time lapse for a voice message?

08:28.000 --> 08:32.000
I think the rocket would be much faster and much more efficient. I know the

08:32.000 --> 08:36.000
exact trajectory anyway. And I'd like to send a message to Commissioner Bell,

08:36.000 --> 08:40.000
and one to the laboratory as well.

08:40.000 --> 08:44.000
Ha!

08:44.000 --> 08:48.000
Grady, I feel like a million dollars.

08:48.000 --> 08:52.000
Never mind bringing me any mess. And incidentally,

08:52.000 --> 08:56.000
I've had news from Blakeslee. He's hot on the trail of Dr. Clark.

08:56.000 --> 09:00.000
Good man, that Blakeslee. Even with all his

09:00.000 --> 09:04.000
yikes and pip-pips and so on.

09:04.000 --> 09:08.000
Commissioner Bell? Oh, it's better to haul the wreckage. Hey, uh, you heard

09:08.000 --> 09:12.000
anything from Captain Video? Wouldn't you like to know?

09:12.000 --> 09:16.000
Now, listen to me. That broadcast you made was a phony, Commissioner. You told the people

09:16.000 --> 09:20.000
that Captain Video and the Rangers are still alive. They'd soon appear in person.

09:20.000 --> 09:24.000
That's right. Well, I happen to know that's

09:24.000 --> 09:28.000
impossible. I checked all the astronomical sources

09:28.000 --> 09:32.000
and that planet Metisero can't even be seen. You know, my column's gonna

09:32.000 --> 09:36.000
say that you've rigged up identical doubles for Captain Video and the Rangers too.

09:36.000 --> 09:40.000
And that you'll show these doubles to all the people just to delude them. You know that you're

09:40.000 --> 09:44.000
right, Hall. Except that we didn't hire doubles.

09:44.000 --> 09:48.000
We hired the twin brothers of the Captain and the Rangers. Why?

09:48.000 --> 09:52.000
Huh?

09:52.000 --> 09:56.000
Commissioner Bell calling Jordan,

09:56.000 --> 10:00.000
identifying number 704. Come in, Jordan. Uh, Jordan, station one,

10:00.000 --> 10:04.000
numero 104. Go ahead, Commissioner. Jordan, I've only had one rocket message

10:04.000 --> 10:08.000
from Captain Video. Have there been any more? No, Commissioner, but our instruments are

10:08.000 --> 10:12.000
registering the same electric charge as they showed before the first rocket landed.

10:12.000 --> 10:16.000
Now, that should mean that another rocket is on the way. Good, then, uh, contact me,

10:16.000 --> 10:20.000
Jordan, when it lands. I certainly will. Jordan, signing off.

10:20.000 --> 10:24.000
Commission Bell, signing off.

10:24.000 --> 10:28.000
We'll return to Captain Video in one minute.

10:28.000 --> 10:32.000
You know, Video Rangers, if you ask almost anybody,

10:32.000 --> 10:36.000
who was Betsy Ross? Quick as a wink, they'll tell you.

10:36.000 --> 10:40.000
Why she made the first American flag. But how many of us know anything at all

10:40.000 --> 10:44.000
about George Ross, Betsy's uncle by marriage? Well, George Ross was

10:44.000 --> 10:48.000
one of the signers of our Declaration of Independence. One of the men who was

10:48.000 --> 10:52.000
willing to risk charges of treason and death, if need be, to preserve

10:52.000 --> 10:56.000
the rights and privileges of his countrymen. Many times

10:56.000 --> 11:00.000
we take these hard fought for privileges, our American heritage of freedom

11:00.000 --> 11:04.000
of thought and action, for granted. They are so much a part of us

11:04.000 --> 11:08.000
that we feel they never could be taken away. But in the world today,

11:08.000 --> 11:12.000
there are those who would destroy our American heritage, who would tear down

11:12.000 --> 11:16.000
our ideals, trample underfoot the flag that came into being

11:16.000 --> 11:20.000
under the skillful fingers of Betsy Ross. So let's be alert

11:20.000 --> 11:24.000
and realize as Americans that freedom is everybody's

11:24.000 --> 11:28.000
job, Video Rangers. Now let's get back to our story.

11:28.000 --> 11:32.000
As communications rockets splashed with

11:32.000 --> 11:36.000
the speed of light between metasteros and Earth, the remote carrier beam was

11:36.000 --> 11:40.000
functioning swiftly too, as it brought Captain Video's special agent

11:40.000 --> 11:44.000
into sharp focus.

11:44.000 --> 11:48.000
...

11:48.000 --> 11:52.000
...

11:52.000 --> 11:56.000
...

11:56.000 --> 12:00.000
What's happened here? I reckon you know it, you wouldn't

12:00.000 --> 12:04.000
be here. Which one of you is Turner? I'm Turner.

12:04.000 --> 12:08.000
The Callahan girl brought word that a fellow named the whistler

12:08.000 --> 12:12.000
murdered Jerry Blake. There's a few things

12:12.000 --> 12:16.000
wrong with those remarks. In the first place, Miss Callahan never said it was

12:16.000 --> 12:20.000
murder. In the second place, my name... Never mind that.

12:20.000 --> 12:24.000
You killed a man. The sheriff called it murder, and I

12:24.000 --> 12:28.000
call it murder, and we hang murders in this county. Now what do you think

12:28.000 --> 12:32.000
of that? No use getting hard about it. You're a

12:32.000 --> 12:36.000
posse, not a lynching mob. And the sheriff here is an officer of the law.

12:36.000 --> 12:40.000
The sheriff will do what I say. I'm running this.

12:40.000 --> 12:44.000
I sort of figured that way. Alright, what's next?

12:44.000 --> 12:48.000
Unbuckle your gun belt, Mr. U.S. Marshal. So you know me.

12:48.000 --> 12:52.000
Yeah, we know you're alright, but no one

12:52.000 --> 12:56.000
can ever prove we knew you to be anything but a murdered, resistant

12:56.000 --> 13:00.000
arrest. You'll never take my guns except in smoke.

13:00.000 --> 13:04.000
The six rifles out there drawn a beat on you right now.

13:04.000 --> 13:08.000
Only six?

13:08.000 --> 13:12.000
Well, I thought there must be a dozen of them, judging by the noise they made

13:12.000 --> 13:16.000
gliding through the bridge. Well, I reckon you've got me.

13:20.000 --> 13:24.000
Drop that gun!

13:24.000 --> 13:28.000
Tell your friends behind me not to move, or you four will drop!

13:28.000 --> 13:32.000
Don't worry, Whistler. If one of them should move,

13:32.000 --> 13:36.000
his light will go out quick. Drop those guns, you homebren.

13:44.000 --> 13:48.000
Get off them horses and get out in the open.

13:48.000 --> 13:58.000
That'll be far enough.

13:58.000 --> 14:00.000
March on down there.

14:00.000 --> 14:20.000
March on down there. Pronto!

14:30.000 --> 14:38.000
Stop right there. Get a room, Tommy.

14:54.000 --> 14:58.000
Yes? This is Victor, Dr. Pauli.

14:58.000 --> 15:02.000
Yes, yes. I've completed the atomic disintegrator according to the plans you gave me.

15:02.000 --> 15:08.000
Well, then, bring it in. I want it immediately. Why waste my time with telephone calls?

15:18.000 --> 15:22.000
This is Dr. Pauli.

15:22.000 --> 15:28.000
This is Dr. Pauli.

15:28.000 --> 15:34.000
That's right. Ah, yes.

15:34.000 --> 15:40.000
My ultra-planetary fence never is as except as I knew it would be.

15:40.000 --> 15:52.000
Yes, now. Now to fill the whole sky until contact with Ultima Oriens is established.

15:54.000 --> 16:02.000
This is Dr. Pauli calling Ultima Oriens in the outer limits.

16:02.000 --> 16:08.000
Dr. Pauli to Ultima Oriens.

16:08.000 --> 16:12.000
Captain Dilly and the Video Ranger, come here quickly!

16:12.000 --> 16:14.000
What is it, Tommy? Listen.

16:14.000 --> 16:22.000
This is Dr. Pauli calling Ultima Oriens in the outer limits.

16:22.000 --> 16:26.000
This is Dr. Pauli to Ultima Oriens.

16:26.000 --> 16:28.000
Pauli, I wonder what's happened to Blakley.

16:28.000 --> 16:32.000
Dr. Pauli's alive and I'm loose again, sir. We've got to call off this trip to CERN.

16:32.000 --> 16:36.000
No, Ranger, we've still got to go to CERN. Blakley hasn't let us down yet.

16:36.000 --> 16:38.000
Excuse me.

16:38.000 --> 16:40.000
Yes?

16:40.000 --> 16:44.000
Interplanetary trip reporting. A rocket from Earth has just landed.

16:44.000 --> 16:48.000
Bring it here as soon as it cools. It will be brought.

16:48.000 --> 16:50.000
Right.

16:50.000 --> 16:52.000
We'll have to wait and see what's in this rocket.

16:52.000 --> 16:54.000
It's probably an answer from Commissioner Bell.

16:54.000 --> 16:56.000
How about your trip to Turson, Captain?

16:56.000 --> 17:00.000
I don't want to take long before that rocket cools. We'll be able to read the message right away.

17:00.000 --> 17:04.000
Go ahead. Call Regus and tell him we're starting right away.

17:04.000 --> 17:06.000
Yes, sir.

17:08.000 --> 17:12.000
Hermes Lycos calling Regus of Turson.

17:12.000 --> 17:16.000
Hermes Lycos calling Regus of Turson. Regus in demand.

17:16.000 --> 17:20.000
This is Regus of Turson.

17:20.000 --> 17:26.000
Regus, Captain Video and the Video Ranger will be on their way to you within a half a time cycle.

17:26.000 --> 17:28.000
Excellent.

17:28.000 --> 17:34.000
I shall see that a proper welcome is prepared for Captain Video.

17:34.000 --> 17:38.000
What means of transportation are they going to use?

17:38.000 --> 17:40.000
In one of my orbit control units.

17:40.000 --> 17:44.000
Excellent. Excellent.

17:44.000 --> 17:50.000
I shall be certain to treat Captain Video as he deserves to be treated.

17:50.000 --> 17:54.000
This is Regus of Turson signing off.

17:54.000 --> 17:58.000
This is Hermes Lycos signing off.

17:58.000 --> 18:02.000
Hi. Hi.

18:04.000 --> 18:08.000
The address calling Earth in the eight time cycle.

18:08.000 --> 18:12.000
Moro to Dr. Pauley. Respond.

18:12.000 --> 18:16.000
This is Dr. Pauley. I am receiving you.

18:16.000 --> 18:20.000
Good. I am Moro, Chief of the Army to Uthama Oren.

18:20.000 --> 18:22.000
Ah, yes.

18:22.000 --> 18:26.000
Uthama Oren welcomes this contact with you, Dr. Pauley.

18:26.000 --> 18:30.000
She would speak to you personally, but she is busy with inner planetary affairs.

18:30.000 --> 18:32.000
Ah, yes, I see. I see.

18:32.000 --> 18:36.000
Tell me, what have you learned about the planet Metasteras?

18:36.000 --> 18:39.000
Metasteras is in excellent condition.

18:39.000 --> 18:42.000
Burning its orbit, safe from attack.

18:42.000 --> 18:44.000
What?

18:44.000 --> 18:47.000
I, my first report, told me that it had been blasted.

18:47.000 --> 18:49.000
On the contrary, Dr. Pauley.

18:49.000 --> 18:54.000
From what we have heard of the over short wave, it is certain that it is in great danger.

18:54.000 --> 18:57.000
Through the intervention of Captain Video.

18:57.000 --> 19:01.000
Ah, Captain Video. That is what I wanted to talk to Uthama about.

19:01.000 --> 19:03.000
I wish to visit her.

19:03.000 --> 19:10.000
Perhaps I can help her annex Metasteras and Turson and kill Captain Video as we do it.

19:10.000 --> 19:14.000
Uthama Oren will welcome your visit.

19:14.000 --> 19:17.000
Excellent. Excellent.

19:17.000 --> 19:22.000
I shall use atomic integration, same as I did the last time.

19:22.000 --> 19:25.000
Good. I will switch on the atom generator.

19:25.000 --> 19:28.000
You will be reassembled whenever you wish.

19:28.000 --> 19:32.000
Ah, excellent. Excellent. Everything is ready here on Earth.

19:32.000 --> 19:35.000
I will wait until the sun has seen it.

19:35.000 --> 19:40.000
No. You had better wait until the sun has reached the focal point of the Earth before it.

19:40.000 --> 19:44.000
Otherwise, the intense heat will scatter your atoms beyond total reassembly.

19:44.000 --> 19:46.000
Ah, yes. Yes. Good.

19:46.000 --> 19:49.000
Then signal me when everything is ready.

19:49.000 --> 19:53.000
Understood. Moral of the line, Lord.

19:53.000 --> 19:55.000
Dr. Foley, signal.

19:55.000 --> 19:58.000
Ah.

19:58.000 --> 20:13.000
How is Captain Video going to feel when he learns that I, Dr. Foley, his vicarious enemy, has also reached the outer limits?

20:13.000 --> 20:17.000
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha.

20:17.000 --> 20:21.000
We'll get back to Captain Video in one minute.

20:21.000 --> 20:25.000
Rangers ever tackle a job you really look forward to doing?

20:25.000 --> 20:30.000
Oh, boy, you say, rubbing your hands together. That's for me. That's right up my alley.

20:30.000 --> 20:34.000
Well, there's one big job that's right up everybody's alley, Rangers.

20:34.000 --> 20:36.000
That's the job of fighting discrimination.

20:36.000 --> 20:42.000
Seeing to it that the next fellow gets a fair chance, regardless of his race or religion.

20:42.000 --> 20:45.000
We've got a talent for that, if we know how to use it.

20:45.000 --> 20:47.000
It comes under the heading of friendship.

20:47.000 --> 20:53.000
When we like people and are genuinely interested in them, there's no room for un-American prejudice.

20:53.000 --> 20:56.000
So all we have to do is to keep on making new friends.

20:56.000 --> 20:58.000
Easy as pie.

20:58.000 --> 21:02.000
There's another reason why fighting discrimination ought to be up everybody's alley.

21:02.000 --> 21:10.000
Because those who turn thumbs down on one race or religion one day are just as apt to turn against another race or religion another day.

21:10.000 --> 21:12.000
Yours maybe, who knows?

21:12.000 --> 21:17.000
So when you fight for an equal chance for everyone in your club, on your team, in jobs of all kinds,

21:17.000 --> 21:20.000
you're fighting your own battle too, Rangers.

21:20.000 --> 21:25.000
Now back to Captain Video.

21:25.000 --> 21:30.000
As Dr. Pauley spun his sinister plot back to the Mountain Laboratory,

21:30.000 --> 21:33.000
the scanning equipment showed other plots, another intrigue,

21:33.000 --> 21:53.000
as Captain Video's special agent battled for his life.

21:53.000 --> 21:55.000
You there, hard guy.

21:55.000 --> 21:58.000
Step out in front.

21:58.000 --> 22:08.000
Tie a rope around his neck. Make sure it don't choke you.

22:08.000 --> 22:10.000
Tie his hands too, Tommy.

22:10.000 --> 22:12.000
He's the big boss.

22:12.000 --> 22:26.000
We'll let him lead the parade.

22:26.000 --> 22:31.000
You there, handsome.

22:56.000 --> 23:04.000
Okay, General, march your troops back to town.

23:04.000 --> 23:06.000
You can't get away with this, fella.

23:06.000 --> 23:08.000
Get going or I'll make you double time it.

23:08.000 --> 23:10.000
Don't yank.

23:10.000 --> 23:19.000
Shut up.

23:19.000 --> 23:26.000
Hey, mister, I can't walk the town. I got fallen arches.

23:49.000 --> 24:06.000
You might as well have turned a bunch of rattlesnakes loose in your backyard, Whistler.

24:06.000 --> 24:11.000
There isn't a one of those citizens that'll get a good night's sleep till they're both rubbed off.

24:11.000 --> 24:13.000
And thanks, Tommy, for saving me.

24:13.000 --> 24:15.000
I couldn't have held them off all alone.

24:15.000 --> 24:20.000
You had them in hand before I brought it in.

24:20.000 --> 24:22.000
That only friends, Captain.

24:22.000 --> 24:27.000
That must be the rocket message, no?

24:27.000 --> 24:29.000
Thank you, Philippa.

24:29.000 --> 24:37.000
Here we are, Captain.

24:37.000 --> 24:39.000
A little bit worse for wear, but...

24:39.000 --> 24:41.000
Oh, it's been Commissioner Bell, all right.

24:41.000 --> 24:43.000
What did he say?

24:43.000 --> 24:45.000
He congratulates us.

24:45.000 --> 24:47.000
Wants us to get home right away.

24:47.000 --> 24:48.000
Says the price is after us.

24:48.000 --> 24:49.000
Oh, really?

24:49.000 --> 24:50.000
As it always is.

24:50.000 --> 24:52.000
He says Dr. Pauley is causing trouble again.

24:52.000 --> 24:55.000
Hopefully he can take care of Dr. Pauley again.

24:55.000 --> 24:58.000
He's going to have to, Richard.

24:58.000 --> 25:00.000
He'll get back.

25:00.000 --> 25:04.000
Send Mr. Bell a reply, eh?

25:04.000 --> 25:06.000
Tell him.

25:06.000 --> 25:09.000
He says he's got to ride with us.

25:09.000 --> 25:11.000
He's knackered.

25:11.000 --> 25:13.000
He's pretty tight.

25:13.000 --> 25:15.000
Thomas Brakesley.

25:15.000 --> 25:19.000
He's referred everything to Brakesley, and so we decide.

25:19.000 --> 25:24.000
Now, Pruitt, will your rocket launching department get this up right away?

25:24.000 --> 25:26.000
I will attend to it myself, Captain.

25:26.000 --> 25:27.000
All right.

25:27.000 --> 25:30.000
And while you're doing that, do you mind if I contact orbit control?

25:30.000 --> 25:32.000
Oh, you did not ask, Captain.

25:32.000 --> 25:35.000
My laboratory and everything in it is completely yours.

25:35.000 --> 25:37.000
All right.

25:37.000 --> 25:40.000
All right, you're going to have to make this a short trip to Turson.

25:40.000 --> 25:43.000
Because I also want to stop off at the planet Mars.

25:43.000 --> 25:45.000
I want to study the structure of that planet.

25:45.000 --> 25:47.000
And teach C to the O-1 too, eh?

25:47.000 --> 25:48.000
Maybe we can.

25:48.000 --> 25:50.000
Captain Video to orbit control.

25:50.000 --> 25:52.000
Come in, orbit control.

25:52.000 --> 25:54.000
Captain Video calling orbit control.

25:54.000 --> 25:58.000
Control, orbit control reporting to Captain Video.

25:58.000 --> 26:00.000
Everything set for our trip?

26:00.000 --> 26:02.000
Everything is ready, Captain.

26:02.000 --> 26:05.000
The rocket is fueled and waiting for you.

26:05.000 --> 26:06.000
All right.

26:06.000 --> 26:07.000
We'll be right there.

26:07.000 --> 26:08.000
That's all.

26:08.000 --> 26:09.000
Captain Video signing off.

26:09.000 --> 26:11.000
Okay, right there.

26:11.000 --> 26:13.000
Off to Turson.

26:13.000 --> 26:15.000
Right.

26:15.000 --> 26:17.000
Ah, signal.

26:17.000 --> 26:19.000
Trapped for Captain Video's set?

26:19.000 --> 26:22.000
Everything is ready, Ray.

26:22.000 --> 26:24.000
Good.

26:24.000 --> 26:26.000
And we best be off to the landing stage.

26:26.000 --> 26:28.000
And signal.

26:28.000 --> 26:31.000
Remember, be sure to act casually.

26:31.000 --> 26:34.000
And if there was nothing the matter at all,

26:34.000 --> 26:36.000
we don't want them to suspect a thing.

26:36.000 --> 26:40.000
By the way, Reagan, I just overheard an ultra-short wave message

26:40.000 --> 26:42.000
from someone named Dr. Pauli.

26:42.000 --> 26:45.000
He was trying to reach Ultima Aureus.

26:45.000 --> 26:47.000
Dr. Pauli.

26:47.000 --> 26:50.000
Dr. Pauli.

26:50.000 --> 26:52.000
I know that name.

26:52.000 --> 26:57.000
He's the Earth man who managed to make the interplanetary passage

26:57.000 --> 26:59.000
by disintegration.

26:59.000 --> 27:02.000
Ultima Aureus, of course.

27:02.000 --> 27:05.000
That's who should be here when Captain Video is on the move.

27:05.000 --> 27:08.000
That's who should be here when Captain Video arrives.

27:08.000 --> 27:11.000
Yes.

27:11.000 --> 27:14.000
Contact her immediately.

27:14.000 --> 27:18.000
Tell her that I want her here as soon as she possibly can.

27:18.000 --> 27:21.000
Yes.

27:21.000 --> 27:27.000
We shall not only set a trap for Captain Video,

27:27.000 --> 27:29.000
we shall have some fun.

27:29.000 --> 27:32.000
Tell her to be sure to disguise herself.

27:32.000 --> 27:38.000
So completely that not even Captain Video and his ranger will recognize her.

27:38.000 --> 27:41.000
Tell her to be out of the limit.

27:41.000 --> 27:43.000
The seventh time cycle.

27:43.000 --> 27:46.000
Take them calling Ultima Aureus.

27:46.000 --> 27:48.000
Yes.

27:48.000 --> 28:02.000
Things are really starting to happen now, Video Rangers.

28:02.000 --> 28:05.000
Will the fabulous Ultima Aureus come to Turson?

28:05.000 --> 28:08.000
And will Captain Video pierce her disguise

28:08.000 --> 28:11.000
and avoid the stunning trap that's been set for her?

28:11.000 --> 28:15.000
Well, we'll have the answers to those questions next time we meet, Video Rangers.

28:15.000 --> 28:25.000
And same station for Captain Video and his Video Rangers.

28:25.000 --> 28:27.000
Captain Video is played by Richard Coogan.

28:27.000 --> 28:29.000
Video Ranger by Don Hastings.

28:29.000 --> 28:31.000
Dr. Polly by Hal Conklin.

28:31.000 --> 28:35.000
Captain Video is written by M.C. Brock and directed by Larry White.

28:35.000 --> 28:41.000
Your announcer has been Greg Scott.

28:41.000 --> 28:46.000
This is the Newmont Television Network.

